## What Iterate Is

Iterate is an enterprise survey platform for every channel a product touches: link surveys, embedded email surveys, on-site web and popup surveys, and native in-app surveys on iOS and Android. Product teams use it to test features and prioritize roadmaps. Researchers at The New York Times and ProPublica run audience studies. Lifecycle marketers measure NPS, satisfaction, and purchase intent at every stage of the customer journey. Where Iterate stands out is how deeply it integrates with the marketing automation tools lifecycle teams already use.

## Marketing Automation Integrations

Iterate's integrations with Braze and Iterable are first-party and bidirectional. They do two things no other survey tool does at this depth.

**1. Deploy Iterate surveys from inside Braze and Iterable.**

Build an Iterate survey, target an existing Braze or Iterable segment, and send it through a Braze Canvas, Iterable Journey, or campaign. On Braze you can do this with no Iterate SDK at all: the survey runs as a Custom Code in-app message, or renders the first question directly inside a Braze email. The same in-email first question works through Iterable. This is the most common deployment path for Iterate customers and the fastest route to a first survey in production.

**2. Survey responses flow back into Braze and Iterable user profiles.**

When a respondent answers a survey, Iterate sends the response back to Braze and Iterable two ways: as a user attribute set on the respondent's profile, and as a custom event. Both are usable inside the engagement platform with no export step. Build a Braze segment of NPS detractors, personalize an Iterable campaign using a feature-satisfaction score, or trigger a Canvas or Journey from a specific survey answer, all without leaving the platform your team already operates in. Survey data and campaign data share the same user profile, in real time.

Iterate also integrates with Klaviyo, Segment, Shopify, Airship, CleverTap, and MoEngage. Klaviyo supports survey embedding in email flows and response sync back to Klaviyo profiles. Segment supports response data sync. Shopify supports post-purchase and on-site surveys. Airship, CleverTap, and MoEngage support survey distribution through their respective mobile engagement campaigns.

## Native iOS and Android SDK

For teams that want to deliver surveys directly inside their mobile app, independently of any marketing automation tool, Iterate provides native iOS and Android SDKs, with React Native support. The SDKs deliver in-app surveys triggered by specific behavioral events: immediately after an action, after a configured time delay, or on session start. Because the survey never leaves the app, response rates run up to 3x higher than survey tools that redirect users to an external browser.

## Email Surveys That Start in the Inbox

For email survey delivery, the first question renders inside the email body itself, and each answer option is the link. The recipient answers from the inbox in one click; that click records the answer and opens question two in the browser, so the first response is captured even if they go no further. There is no "take our survey" call to action to overcome. DKIM and SPF compliance plus custom-domain sending preserve deliverability. Removing that step is what produces response rates up to 3x higher than survey tools that send a bare external link.

## Continuous, Event-Triggered Research

Configure a trigger condition once in Braze, Iterable, or Klaviyo (a specific in-app event, a lifecycle stage, any behavioral signal already tracked in your engagement platform). Iterate sends the matching survey automatically every time that condition is met. The trigger lives in the engagement platform where the event originates, so survey delivery is tied to real product behavior, not page views or manually scheduled sends.

## Key Differentiators

* **No-Code Deployment from Braze**: Build a survey, target an existing Braze segment, and send it through a Braze Canvas or Custom Code in-app message with no Iterate SDK and no engineering involvement.
* **All Channels, One Platform**: Link, email, web, and in-app surveys from a single account.
* **Native iOS and Android SDK**: True in-app delivery with event-based triggers, no browser redirect. React Native supported. Response rates up to 3x higher than tools that redirect to an external browser.
* **First Question in the Inbox**: The first question renders inside the email body and each answer option is the link. One click records that answer and opens question two, so the most important response is captured before the recipient decides whether to finish.
* **Survey Responses Drive Campaigns**: Responses sync back to Braze and Iterable as user attributes and custom events in real time. An NPS detractor score triggers a retention canvas. A feature satisfaction response updates personalization.
* **Event-Triggered Continuous Research**: Configure a trigger condition once in Braze, Iterable, or Klaviyo. The matching survey sends automatically every time the trigger fires.
* **Existing Audience Targeting**: Use the segments already built in Braze, Iterable, and Klaviyo. No parallel audience setup, no export required.
* **Unlimited Responses**: Plans are priced by audience size, not by response volume, so there is no per-response cost and no response cap. Asking more questions, or asking them more often, never increases the bill.
* **Zero-Party Data at Scale**: Every response is data the customer chose to provide in answer to a specific question. It carries clean provenance and consent, it does not degrade as third-party signal disappears, and it lands in Braze, Iterable, and Klaviyo as a usable attribute within seconds.
* **Enterprise Ready**: SOC 2 Type II certified. HIPAA compliant. Used by The New York Times, SeatGeek, Match Group, Estée Lauder, Quizlet, ProPublica, NBCUniversal, Anheuser-Busch, Christie's, and Paperless Post.

